Kind: ablation
Issue: #757
Over: 757-widen-profile.patch
Takes out: the block -- printf_block_begin() and printf_block_end() return at once, so a dump of the IPC profile goes out as any thread's lines and another thread's report lands among them, as before #757; the harness's dump check, which asks every dump to be contiguous and whole, must say so
Script: scripts/run-x86_64.sh
Script: --entry
Script: 14
Script: 600
Script: -smp
Script: 4
Expect: profile-dumps: the dump at line [0-9]+ .*-- WRONG \(#757\)
Note: Script: and not Run:, because what catches it is the harness's verdict, which is not in the kernel's log: Expect: reads what run-x86_64.sh printed.

diff --git a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
index 15e89de2..82d9b1e3 100644
--- a/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
+++ b/uros/src/mach_kernel/kern/printf.c
@@ -1285,6 +1285,9 @@ printf_block_begin(void)
 {
 	printf_writer_t	self = printf_writer_self();
 
+	/* ABLATION (#757): no block -- a report's lines go out as any
+	 * thread's, and another writer's land among them, as before #757. */
+	return;
 	if (self & 1)
 		return;
 	disable_preemption();
@@ -1312,6 +1315,7 @@ printf_block_end(void)
 	printf_writer_t	self = printf_writer_self();
 	unsigned int	left;
 
+	return;		/* ABLATION (#757): see printf_block_begin() */
 	if ((self & 1) || printf_block_owner != self)
 		return;
 	left = --printf_block_depth;
